    {
      "note": "Rule 66's compound arm: eirenopoieo is one Greek compound whose two English words each gloss one of its elements - peace answers to eireno-, made to -poieo - so the head is the verbal core made and not the incorporated object, even though English syntax puts the core first and the object in the complement. This brings the unit into line with COL.1.6 and COL.1.10, where karpophoreo heads on bearing. Rule 17's make + complement reading, which headed this unit on peace, is the contrast rule 91 already states and does not reach here: in make straight, make known and make request no part of the English verb glosses the lexeme, whereas made glosses -poieo.",
